cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "chicago_crime_forecast: month-ahead forecasts for 1,000 parallel crime-by-ward time series"
abstract: >-
  A forecasting pipeline that turns the City of Chicago's public incident feed
  into month-ahead counts for every crime-type-and-ward pair in the city: 1,000
  short, seasonal, individually thin series forecast together by a single
  skforecast recursive multi-series model with an XGBoost regressor underneath.
  Accuracy is measured by rolling-origin backtest at a four-month horizon, so
  the reported error is out-of-sample. Built end-to-end with Claude Code and
  published with interactive exploration and validation dashboards.
type: software
